//Rules for naming variables in C++:

//1. Variable names can only contain letters, numbers, and underscores. 
//2. Variable names must begin with a letter or an underscore.
//3. Variable names are case sensitive (myVar and myvar are different variables).
//4. Variable names cannot be a reserved keyword (like int, float, return, etc.).
//5. Variable names should be descriptive and meaningful to improve code readability.
//6. Variable names should not contain spaces or special characters (like @, #, $, %, etc.).
//7. Variable names should not start with a number.

